span="1" colspan="1"> </td><td valign="top" align="left" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Severe adverse events<sup><xref rid="tfn5-jos-2023-00668" ref-type="table-fn">ǁ</xref></sup></td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7 (17.5)</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">2 (5.0)</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.25 (0.05 to 1.28)</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.10</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.26 (0.05 to 1.37)</td><td valign="top" align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">0.11</td></tr></tbody></table><table-wrap-foot><fn><p>Data are presented as n (%) or median (interquartile range).</p><p>TNK, tenecteplase; CI, confidence interval; mRS, modified Rankin Scale; NIHSS, National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale; ENI, early neurological improvement; sICH, symptomatic intracranial hemorrhage; HT, proportion of hemorrhagic transformation; HI, hemorrhagic infarct; PH, parenchymal hemorrhage; NA, not available.</p></fn><fn id="tfn1-jos-2023-00668"><label>*</label><p>Adjusted for key prognostic covariates (age, sex, systolic blood pressure, ischemic stroke, NIHSS score at admission and time from stroke onset to randomization);</p></fn><fn id="tfn2-jos-2023-00668"><label>†</label><p>Analyzed by ordinal logistical regression analysis;</p></fn><fn id="tfn3-jos-2023-00668"><label>‡</label><p>3 Patients in the TNK group died after 14 days and the causes of death were cardiac failure, cerebral hernia induced by massive cerebral infarction, undetermined cause, respectively;</p></fn><fn id="tfn4-jos-2023-00668"><label>§</label><p>Adverse events included dyslipidemia, myocardial infarction, deep vein thrombosis, hypoproteinemia, hyperuricemia, pneumonia, diabetes, appendicitis, urinary infection, periapical inflammation, constipation, hyperhomocysteinemia, etc;</p></fn><fn id="tfn5-jos-2023-00668"><label>ǁ</label><p>Severe adverse events included carotid artery stenosis, intracranial hemorrhage, massive cerebral infarction, recurrent stroke, heart failure, etc.</p></fn></table-wrap-foot></table-wrap></floats-group></article>